WEBVTT

00:00:09.750 --> 00:00:19.560
<b>LEGEND</b>

00:00:09.750 --> 00:00:19.560
<b>OF THE</b>

00:00:09.750 --> 00:00:19.560
<b>  GALACTIC HEROES</b>

00:01:39.620 --> 00:01:46.250
Silver-White Valley

00:01:39.620 --> 00:01:46.250
Chapter 4

00:01:57.330 --> 00:01:58.970
What happened to
Lieutenant Hugenberch ?

00:01:58.970 --> 00:02:00.770
He was supposed to
rendezvous with you.

00:02:01.680 --> 00:02:03.160
I wasn't aware of that.

00:02:03.160 --> 00:02:07.420
Maybe he encountered
enemy troops like we did ?

00:02:07.420 --> 00:02:11.280
Fortunately, we defeated
the enemy, but...

00:02:12.300 --> 00:02:14.700
But why do that ?

00:02:14.700 --> 00:02:17.840
I thought we'd been given an order
to do the reconnaissance on our own.

00:02:17.840 --> 00:02:19.930
I hadn't heard
we'd have backup.

00:02:21.870 --> 00:02:23.420
Oh, well...

00:02:23.420 --> 00:02:26.630
In the end, I felt it would be
unsafe for you all by yourselves.

00:02:27.220 --> 00:02:28.690
I suppose it was
an unnecessary worry.

00:02:29.870 --> 00:02:31.620
More importantly, Commander...

00:02:31.620 --> 00:02:35.240
...from the navigation data we obtained
from the enemy armored vehicle...

00:02:35.240 --> 00:02:37.820
...we should be able
to locate the enemy base.

00:02:38.520 --> 00:02:42.140
Why don't we turn the tables and carry out a surprise attack of our own ?

00:02:43.030 --> 00:02:44.170
Of our own ?

00:02:44.700 --> 00:02:48.750
The enemy committed a great number
of troops to their recent attack.

00:02:49.480 --> 00:02:53.510
Now that they are lost to them,
their base must be thin defensively.

00:02:54.440 --> 00:02:57.640
But we suffered quite
a bit of damage ourselves.

00:02:57.640 --> 00:03:00.860
Nonetheless, right now,
we can still use the tactic...

00:03:00.860 --> 00:03:04.560
...of neutralizing the computer system
that they use in their armored vehicles.

00:03:05.150 --> 00:03:07.360
Given time, they'll
change their codes.

00:03:08.150 --> 00:03:11.530
In that case, I would think we
shouldn't miss this opportunity.

00:03:16.750 --> 00:03:18.450
He doesn't know anything ?

00:03:21.080 --> 00:03:23.750
So it was actually the enemy
who took out Hugenberch ?

00:03:25.050 --> 00:03:27.870
If that's the case,
I still have a chance.

00:03:29.560 --> 00:03:30.910
How does that sound, Captain ?

00:03:33.100 --> 00:03:35.430
It'll be easier
to do during battle.

00:03:38.580 --> 00:03:39.570
Very well.

00:03:39.570 --> 00:03:42.560
We'll immediately organize our
troops and head toward their base.

00:03:44.510 --> 00:03:46.610
You two should
come along as guides.

00:03:48.170 --> 00:03:48.960
Yes, sir.

00:04:09.460 --> 00:04:10.930
How did it go ?

00:04:12.010 --> 00:04:13.380
He fell for
it so easily.

00:04:13.930 --> 00:04:19.470
He'll most likely try to take advantage of the
confusion on the battlefield to fulfill his objective.

00:04:19.910 --> 00:04:21.900
That'll be our chance.

00:04:21.900 --> 00:04:28.410
But isn't it too dangerous for
you to act as a decoy like this ?

00:04:28.410 --> 00:04:31.450
That's why I want
you to watch my back.

00:04:31.450 --> 00:04:35.220
Because of you, I can
take on any kind of risk.

00:04:35.220 --> 00:04:36.630
But...

00:04:37.070 --> 00:04:39.820
You know that some
risks are unavoidable.

00:04:39.820 --> 00:04:44.670
Unless we catch Herder in the act,
we won't be able to get to Benemunde.

00:04:45.420 --> 00:04:46.930
There's no other
way around it.

00:04:46.930 --> 00:04:48.240
I understand.

00:04:48.240 --> 00:04:50.000
I will protect
you at all costs.

00:04:50.720 --> 00:04:51.920
I'm counting on you.

00:05:55.550 --> 00:06:04.360
We've located the base of these rebels, who call themselves the Free Planets Alliance, at point M54, B126.

00:06:04.360 --> 00:06:10.820
The location is in this mountainous region where 
one side is a steep slope, and the other faces a cliff.

00:06:10.820 --> 00:06:14.470
Then there's a corridor for
vehicles that runs from east to west.

00:06:15.210 --> 00:06:18.730
Since our mission is
to exterminate the rebels...

00:06:18.730 --> 00:06:21.980
...we can't just attack from one side and
allow them to escape from the other side.

00:06:24.320 --> 00:06:29.030
Therefore, we'll split into two groups,
and attack from both east and west.

00:06:29.030 --> 00:06:31.520
One group will be under the
command of Commander Martel.

00:06:31.940 --> 00:06:35.010
I will personally take
command of the other.

00:06:39.410 --> 00:06:42.480
Our armored vehicle
troops suffered some damage...

00:06:42.480 --> 00:06:46.580
...but it is certain that the enemy
suffered an even greater loss.

00:06:46.580 --> 00:06:49.900
Since we have a numerical advantage,
we mustn't miss this opportunity.

00:06:49.900 --> 00:06:53.290
We'll wipe the enemy forces off the face of this planet once and for all.

00:06:53.290 --> 00:06:55.130
I expect your best efforts.

00:06:56.410 --> 00:06:57.240
Yes, sir.

00:07:00.620 --> 00:07:02.420
What happened to the Captain ?

00:07:02.420 --> 00:07:04.000
He's strangely excited.

00:07:04.710 --> 00:07:08.550
Usually he says it's too cold and
won't even consider leaving the base.

00:07:08.550 --> 00:07:11.430
It doesn't seem
he's exactly "excited."

00:07:11.430 --> 00:07:14.970
Since he suffered quite a bit of damage
from the enemy surprise attack...

00:07:14.970 --> 00:07:17.790
...he needs a big victory or he won't
be able to face the brass back home.

00:07:17.790 --> 00:07:19.770
That's why he's desperate.

00:07:19.770 --> 00:07:22.620
And the pain is, we have
to go along with that.

00:07:22.620 --> 00:07:23.870
Yeah.

00:07:43.320 --> 00:07:44.590
What is it ?

00:07:44.590 --> 00:07:46.590
Ensign Musel, the Captain
is calling for you.

00:07:54.990 --> 00:07:56.850
Ensign Musel reporting.

00:07:58.100 --> 00:07:59.610
Come in and
shut the door.

00:08:16.780 --> 00:08:18.360
What can I do for you ?

00:08:18.360 --> 00:08:21.680
If we use radio communications,
the enemy can detect our location...

00:08:21.680 --> 00:08:23.620
...so I had you
come in person.

00:08:23.620 --> 00:08:26.900
As I was analyzing the data you
brought us, I realized something.

00:08:29.160 --> 00:08:31.360
It's the cliff on the
south side of their base.

00:08:33.060 --> 00:08:36.130
If they take this route, they
could possibly escape on foot.

00:08:37.890 --> 00:08:39.700
That possibility
can't be denied.

00:08:40.470 --> 00:08:41.680
That's right, isn't it ?

00:08:41.680 --> 00:08:45.770
As I said earlier, our mission
is to wipe out the enemy.

00:08:45.770 --> 00:08:49.800
We need to block any route
that could be used for their escape.

00:08:51.070 --> 00:08:53.870
So I want you and
Junior Ensign Kircheis...

00:08:53.870 --> 00:08:57.170
...to go around the mountain
base and block this route.

00:08:57.170 --> 00:08:58.680
On our own ?

00:08:59.840 --> 00:09:02.300
As you know, we can't
afford to send more troops.

00:09:06.080 --> 00:09:07.180
Yes, sir.

00:09:07.180 --> 00:09:10.070
I want to make this clear:
do not use radio transmissions.

00:09:10.070 --> 00:09:12.050
For any communications,
send a messenger.

00:09:12.880 --> 00:09:17.150
When Kircheis leaves the site as a messenger he must be planning to come after me.

00:09:23.620 --> 00:09:25.390
Understood, sir.

00:09:37.010 --> 00:09:40.870
Just as I thought, he ordered
us on a separate mission.

00:09:40.870 --> 00:09:41.510
Then...

00:09:42.080 --> 00:09:45.880
Furthermore, he wants me to be all by
myself and intends to come after me then.

00:09:46.760 --> 00:09:48.310
How obvious.

00:09:48.310 --> 00:09:50.290
But that'll be
our opportunity.

00:09:53.550 --> 00:09:57.810
We killed Hugenberch, but
I want to capture Herder alive.

00:09:57.810 --> 00:10:02.190
And we'll make Herder testify that
Benemunde's the one who's pulling the strings.

00:10:02.190 --> 00:10:07.290
Unless we get to the root of the problem,
it might endanger my sister.

00:10:08.850 --> 00:10:11.840
But I doubt it'll be easy
to get him to testify.

00:10:12.410 --> 00:10:14.320
You're right.

00:10:14.320 --> 00:10:15.960
So I have an idea.

00:10:54.500 --> 00:10:55.520
Commence attack !

00:11:19.650 --> 00:11:21.170
It's begun.

00:11:21.170 --> 00:11:22.680
Just as we expected,
it's earlier than scheduled.

00:11:23.500 --> 00:11:24.420
Let's hurry.

00:11:24.420 --> 00:11:24.900
Right.

00:11:32.370 --> 00:11:34.500
The Alliance Force
resisted fiercely...

00:11:34.500 --> 00:11:37.410
...but robbed of their mobile capacity,
they couldn't hold up for long.

00:11:37.410 --> 00:11:39.280
Eventually, their
counterattack faltered.

00:11:47.010 --> 00:11:47.550
Charge !

00:11:52.160 --> 00:11:53.160
Charge !

00:12:29.090 --> 00:12:30.160
We've arrived.

00:12:31.030 --> 00:12:32.380
Then we'll do as planned.

00:12:33.000 --> 00:12:33.500
Yeah.

00:13:47.710 --> 00:13:48.320
Bastard...

00:13:50.860 --> 00:13:51.550
Don't move !

00:13:52.120 --> 00:13:55.730
I knew you'd take advantage
of the chaos to come after me.

00:13:56.470 --> 00:13:59.900
You thought you had me in your trap,
but you're the one who's trapped.

00:14:01.880 --> 00:14:02.950
How cheeky !

00:14:02.950 --> 00:14:04.990
What can you do
all by yourself ?

00:14:10.400 --> 00:14:11.760
Don't underestimate me !

00:14:13.600 --> 00:14:16.060
I've been through
many battles.

00:14:16.600 --> 00:14:19.970
A brat without battlefield experience
has no chance against me !

00:14:22.180 --> 00:14:26.300
I've staked my life
in battle so many times.

00:14:27.020 --> 00:14:29.950
And through it all, what I finally
got is the position I have now.

00:14:29.950 --> 00:14:33.050
But even that is merely a
commander on the front line !

00:14:33.650 --> 00:14:35.630
On a frontier planet like this,
an icy place without a sun...

00:14:35.630 --> 00:14:39.620
...I don't even know what the future holds for me and I can't even see my family !

00:14:39.620 --> 00:14:43.320
I'm tired of having
to fight like this !

00:14:47.720 --> 00:14:51.940
If I kill you, I'll be able to
go back to the warm mainland.

00:14:52.620 --> 00:14:57.520
After all, you're assured of your future
promotion because of your sister's power !

00:14:58.620 --> 00:15:00.370
You'll never understand me !

00:15:19.070 --> 00:15:21.070
You're too weak !

00:15:40.180 --> 00:15:41.730
This is the end, you brat !

00:16:03.600 --> 00:16:05.620
Are you all right,
Lord Reinhard ?

00:16:07.270 --> 00:16:08.480
Kircheis !

00:16:15.280 --> 00:16:16.810
I won't kill you.

00:16:16.810 --> 00:16:18.170
You're an important
witness, after all.

00:16:18.930 --> 00:16:20.010
Witness...?

00:16:21.370 --> 00:16:26.590
That's right; a witness to testify that it was
Marquise Benemunde who gave you the order.

00:16:26.590 --> 00:16:27.480
What ?

00:16:27.480 --> 00:16:28.550
How do you know that ?

00:16:30.330 --> 00:16:32.980
Hugenberch told us
before he died.

00:16:32.980 --> 00:16:37.460
Of course, he got carried away and talked
too much, and that was his downfall.

00:16:39.530 --> 00:16:42.070
No, I won't testify.

00:16:42.890 --> 00:16:45.520
If I deny it,
there's no evidence.

00:16:45.520 --> 00:16:51.830
Even if you insist that you heard it,
a Captain's testimony or an Ensign's...?

00:16:51.830 --> 00:16:55.620
Which do you think will be given
more weight in a court-martial ?!

00:16:56.120 --> 00:16:57.680
We'll have third-party testimony.

00:17:03.420 --> 00:17:04.790
Junior Ensign Kircheis ?

00:17:04.790 --> 00:17:07.320
He's like your vassal.

00:17:07.320 --> 00:17:10.270
He's not qualified
to be a witness !

00:17:10.270 --> 00:17:11.270
It's not me.

00:17:22.970 --> 00:17:23.960
Martel ?

00:17:23.960 --> 00:17:24.910
Why are you here ?

00:17:26.430 --> 00:17:29.730
The Commander will be the
witness to your statement.

00:17:29.730 --> 00:17:31.780
Kircheis had him
come here for that.

00:17:32.960 --> 00:17:34.580
Do you still intend
to deny it, Captain ?

00:17:39.460 --> 00:17:41.910
I'm the brother of
His Majesty's favored lady.

00:17:41.910 --> 00:17:45.820
Attempting to kill me would incur a
punishment similar to that of high treason.

00:17:46.890 --> 00:17:50.880
Even Marquise Benemunde won't
be able to avoid capital punishment.

00:17:52.530 --> 00:17:53.600
High treason...?

00:17:56.210 --> 00:17:59.060
For high treason...

00:17:59.060 --> 00:18:01.000
...my family will also
get the death penalty...

00:18:17.730 --> 00:18:18.290
Herder !

00:18:33.630 --> 00:18:34.650
Dammit...!

00:18:38.810 --> 00:18:39.770
Commander Martel.

00:18:41.730 --> 00:18:45.650
I'd like to have you testify
to what Captain Herder said here.

00:18:57.060 --> 00:19:03.720
In the battle to capture the enemy
base, Captain Herder died honorably.

00:19:04.580 --> 00:19:08.120
That's what will be
in the official record.

00:19:10.390 --> 00:19:11.210
Commander !

00:19:13.390 --> 00:19:20.070
I will also report that you two made a significant contribution to the conquest of the enemy base.

00:19:20.070 --> 00:19:24.190
You two will get the promotions that you desire and you'll be appointed to a fleet assignment.

00:19:25.730 --> 00:19:29.160
For now, please
be content with that.

00:19:30.520 --> 00:19:34.080
That's the best I can do.

00:19:37.730 --> 00:19:39.060
Lord Reinhard...

00:19:42.480 --> 00:19:47.420
As Martel said, Reinhard and Kircheis
were given a new post shortly afterwards.

00:19:48.240 --> 00:19:53.970
Six months later the Imperial Force's B-III base was again attacked by the Alliance Force...

00:19:53.970 --> 00:19:57.790
...and the base commander, Captain Martel, along with his subordinates, all died without surrendering.

00:20:03.430 --> 00:20:05.360
I'm sorry I couldn't
be of help to you.

00:20:06.220 --> 00:20:09.000
No, you saved me
when I was in danger.

00:20:09.000 --> 00:20:10.720
That's more than enough.

00:20:10.720 --> 00:20:11.520
But...

00:20:13.900 --> 00:20:16.520
Regardless of whom you brought
here, it would have been the same.

00:20:18.780 --> 00:20:23.120
There aren't too many people who want to have anything to do with unnecessary feuds at the Court.

00:20:26.560 --> 00:20:28.090
What's that ?

00:20:28.090 --> 00:20:29.320
It's the planet
next to this one.

00:20:30.450 --> 00:20:32.520
It's a gas giant.

00:20:32.520 --> 00:20:35.320
It's gradually pulling
this planet in...

00:20:35.320 --> 00:20:38.870
...and in several thousand years,
it'll go over the Roche limit.

00:20:38.870 --> 00:20:41.360
Kapche-Lanka will then turn
into asteroid fragments.

00:20:42.770 --> 00:20:43.560
Its name is...

00:20:44.210 --> 00:20:45.670
I remember it now.

00:20:45.670 --> 00:20:47.430
It's Planet Legmiza, isn't it ?

00:20:48.270 --> 00:20:49.100
Yes.

00:20:51.140 --> 00:20:57.400
In the sky above that planet, Reinhard
would later encounter his lifetime rival...

00:20:57.400 --> 00:20:59.150
...but he had no way
of knowing it then.

00:21:00.780 --> 00:21:04.210
If we can get out to space,
I'd say that's good enough.

00:21:05.120 --> 00:21:05.860
Yes.

00:21:05.860 --> 00:21:07.320
Let us go, Lord Reinhard.

00:21:07.870 --> 00:21:10.100
Yeah, let's go, Kircheis.

00:21:10.100 --> 00:21:11.500
To the sea of stars.

00:21:32.010 --> 00:21:33.920
What do you
mean it failed ?

00:21:35.200 --> 00:21:39.820
Now that Captain Herder has died in
battle, there's nothing more we can do.

00:21:39.820 --> 00:21:45.450
We'll have to find someone else who'll take
our orders when the brat gets reassigned.

00:21:46.080 --> 00:21:47.530
That's irritating !

00:21:52.680 --> 00:21:57.780
But still, it's difficult to
find someone we can trust.

00:21:57.780 --> 00:22:00.030
In the unlikely event that
this secret gets out...

00:22:01.120 --> 00:22:04.950
Maybe we ought to send
an assassin from our camp.

00:22:06.140 --> 00:22:09.510
Either way, we must be
judicious about our selection.

00:22:10.190 --> 00:22:11.150
Anyway !

00:22:11.500 --> 00:22:14.390
Kill that brat
as soon as possible !

00:22:14.920 --> 00:22:20.060
And then that wench will suffer so much that she will die of sorrow in the end !

00:22:20.060 --> 00:22:20.980
Isn't that right ?!

00:22:21.770 --> 00:22:22.630
Um, yes.

00:22:23.890 --> 00:22:25.200
That's right.

00:22:25.200 --> 00:22:28.620
Just watch, you brat...

00:22:28.620 --> 00:22:29.970
...you wench !

00:22:31.710 --> 00:22:34.850
Even after this, Marquise
Benemunde's evil hands...

00:22:34.850 --> 00:22:39.390
...would come after Reinhard
and Annerose again and again.

00:22:40.340 --> 00:22:46.240
Reinhard had to wait several more years
before they were entirely free of that danger.

00:22:50.690 --> 00:22:58.190
Reinhard:

00:22:50.690 --> 00:22:58.190
Horikawa Ryo

00:22:58.710 --> 00:23:06.270
Benemunde:

00:22:58.710 --> 00:23:06.270
Fujita Toshiko

